<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n116477" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠφέλ-ῐμος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
		rarely <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Chrm.</u>
			174d
		</span></i> (dub. l.), <i><span class="en">
			<u>R.</u>
			607d
		</span></i>:— <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>helping,
				aiding, useful, serviceable, beneficial,</i> sts. of persons,
			as <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Men.</u>
				98c
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>R.</u>
				461b
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			), <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				2.7.9
			</span></i>: but more freq. of things, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.46
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span> to one, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Ion</u>
				138
			</span></i> (lyr.), <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.44
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.64
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔς τι</span> for a
			purpose, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				3.68
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρὸς τὰς πολιτείας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					607d
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπέρ τινος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.2.34
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρίνειν τι ὠ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὠ.</span> as
			Subst., <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				457d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὑμῖν</span>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὠ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.76
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				E.
			</span></i> l. c.: 
				Comp.
			 and 
				Sup.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος, -ώτατος,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Th.
				1.93
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				461b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				179a
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-μως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Mem.</u>
					4.4.1
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				470a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Chrm.</u>
				163c
			</span></i>: 
				Sup.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτατα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					6.1
				</span></i>
			.</div>
